shape theory.sets : theory.algebra.collection, theory.self-reference, theory.minimal {
  type: theorem
  layer: 0
  """
// Section 18 (Shape Set Theory).
// Sets are collections. ZF axioms follow as corollaries of the
// Emergent Collection Principle.
//
// Definition 18.1: Shape-set = collection (identity shape holding
// members in structural isolation).
// Definition 18.2: Membership = reference, not containment.
//
// Theorem 18.3 (Universal Self-Membership): all shape-sets are
// members of themselves. From mandatory prior-state reference
// specialized to identity shapes.
//
// Theorem 18.5 (Russell's Set Is empty_s): the predicate x not-in x
// has empty extension. R collects nothing. Paradox dissolves.
//
// ZF axioms as theorems: Empty Set (18.6), Extensionality (18.7),
// Pairing (18.8), Union (18.9), Power Set (18.10), Separation (18.11),
// Replacement (18.12), Infinity (18.13). All from Emergent Collection.
//
// Theorem 18.14: Foundation is provably FALSE. Law 1 replaces it.
// Theorem 18.15: Universal set U exists.
// Theorem 18.16: P(U) = U (power set of U is U).
//
// Cantor's diagonal: breaks at the self/non-self membership
// distinction. The diagonal set exists but is empty_s.
//
// Derives from: theory.algebra.collection, theory.self-reference,
//               theory.minimal
  """
}
